{"name":"Creamed Muscat","hex":"#8b6962","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"creamed","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of cream"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["(of a food) prepared with cream."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/creamed"},{"term":"muscat","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A white grape variety; used as table grapes and for making raisins and sweet wine.","The muscatel wine made from these grapes."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/muscat"}],"entries":[{"title":"Muscat","blocks":[{"text":"Muscat is the capital and most populous city of Oman. It is the seat of the Governorate of Muscat. According to the National Centre for Statistics and Information (NCSI), the population of the Muscat Governorate in 2022 was 1.72 million. The metropolitan area includes six provinces, called wilayat, and spans approximately 6,500 km2 (2,500 sq mi). The Hajar Mountains dominate the view from Muscat. The city lies on the Gulf of Oman, near the strategically important Strait of Hormuz. Low-lying white buildings are a typical feature of its architecture. The city's port district of Muttrah, with its corniche and harbour, are at the north-eastern edge of the city. Muscat's economy is dominated by trade, petroleum, liquified natural gas and porting."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Al_Alam_Palace.jpg/330px-Al_Alam_Palace.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muscat","wikidata":"Q3826"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/N%C3%A1b%C5%99e%C5%BE%C3%AD_Matry.jpg/500px-N%C3%A1b%C5%99e%C5%BE%C3%AD_Matry.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/N%C3%A1b%C5%99e%C5%BE%C3%AD_Matry.jpg/1280px-N%C3%A1b%C5%99e%C5%BE%C3%AD_Matry.jpg?